  "body": "Home\nAbout us\nIndustries\nManufacturing and industrial\nArchitecture and Buildings\nServices\nScanning\nScan to BIM\nAs-Built Drafting\n3D Modeling\nBuilding analysis\nBOMA As-Built Digital Plans\nMatterport 3D Virtual Tours\nDigital Twins\nBlog\nCase studies\nContact\nGet in touch\n(514) 606-9604\nEnglish\nen\nFrançais\nfr\nVAC AERO International INC.\n3D Scan and 3D Modeling of an Industrial Facility\nSlide title\nWrite your caption here\nButton\nSlide title\nWrite your caption here\nButton\nSlide title\nWrite your caption here\nButton\nSlide title\nWrite your caption here\nButton\nSlide title\nWrite your caption here\nButton\nSlide title\nWrite your caption here\nButton\nSlide title\nWrite your caption here\nButton\nSlide title\nWrite your caption here\nButton\nSetting the scene\nFounded in 1959 in Oakville, Ontario, as Canadian Vac-Hyd Processing Ltd, VAC AERO International Inc. has established itself as a world leader in heat treatment, brazing and vacuum furnace manufacturing. With over 200 employees spread across four factories, the company is experiencing significant growth and was looking to equip itself better to manage and optimize its production spaces.\nThey contacted pointSpace to provide detailed and up-to-date information about their factory in Dorval for their expansion and management objectives.\nIn a growing\nmanufacturing facility,\naccurately understanding existing spaces is essential to plan expansions, optimize production lines and improve equipment layout. When plans are incomplete, outdated or not detailed enough, layout decisions may rely on estimates, creating risks of coordination issues, efficiency losses or costly rework.\nThrough\n3D scanning\n,\n3D modeling\nand\nfactory drafting\n, pointSpace provides a reliable technical foundation to better visualize constraints, anticipate expansion needs and support layout decisions. The deliverables can be used by engineering, production, maintenance and project management teams to plan interventions with greater accuracy.\nThis approach supports industrial 3D scanning, factory layout planning, industrial facility documentation and manufacturing space optimization needs, which are especially strategic for manufacturing and industrial companies across Canada.\nP\nroposed solutions\nFull-color, high-resolution 3D scan\n2D drawings of the building and its production floor,\nincluding the footprint of all machinery and equipment.\nAutoCAD and PDF format.\n3D plans as built from space:\narchitecture, structure and ground machinery.\nRevit and Inventor formats.\nGains\nThis project allowed our clients to:\n• Simulate different factory layouts for 5S initiatives and production line optimization\n• Improve overall management of the plant and its components\n• Reuse plans for various purposes, such as potential expansion projects\nArticle by\nLouis Dallaire\nA graduate of ÉTS in operations and logistics engineering, Louis is passionate about the industrial world. His goal with pointSpace is to make data management and use accessible, because it's not always necessary to use complex tools to solve simple problems !\nComprehensive Building 3D Scanning & 3D Modeling\nView case study\nContact us !\nLouis Dallaire\nldallaire@pointspace.ca\n(514) 606-9604\nContact Us\nFirst name\nLast name\nEmail\nMessage\nThank you for contacting us.\nWe will get back to you as soon as possible.\nOops, there was an error sending your message.\nPlease try again later.\nShare by:",
